# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# slowapi / limits configuration file (NOT the application .env).
#
# Why this file exists:
#   limits' Config() reads its dotenv file with a plain open() and no
#   encoding argument, so it decodes using the OS locale. On Chinese
#   Windows that locale is cp936 (GBK); the project's backend/.env is
#   UTF-8 with Chinese comments, which made `import quota_limiter`
#   (and therefore `import main`) raise UnicodeDecodeError.
#   quota_limiter.py now points Limiter(config_filename=...) here.
#
# RULES for this file:
#   * Keep it pure ASCII. Never paste Chinese text into it.
#   * Only RATELIMIT_* keys are recognised by slowapi; anything else is
#     ignored, so do NOT duplicate app settings here.
#   * Every key below is intentionally commented out, which means slowapi
#     falls back to the values hard-coded in quota_limiter.py
#     (enabled=True, storage_uri="memory://"). Behaviour is unchanged.
#   * limits' Config does NOT expand ${VAR} and has no shell semantics:
#     write literal values only.
#
# AVAILABLE KNOBS (uncomment + set a literal value to override):
# RATELIMIT_ENABLED=true
# RATELIMIT_STORAGE_URI=memory://
# RATELIMIT_STRATEGY=fixed-window
# RATELIMIT_HEADERS_ENABLED=false
# RATELIMIT_ENVIRONMENT=test
# RATELIMIT_PER_POOL=1
# RATELIMIT_APPLICATION_PATHS=/api/health
# RATELIMIT_TRUST_PROXY=false
